  "strategy": "Elf graveyard aggro (\"Graveyard Perfection\")",
  "colors": "BG",
  "identity": "A BG Elf aggro deck whose creatures are priced as though the graveyard requirement were hard, and which makes it trivial. Creakwood Safewright is a 5/5 body for {1}{B} that enters with three -1/-1 counters and removes one per end step 'if there is an Elf card in your graveyard' — cast on turn 2 it attacks as a 3/3 on turn 3 and reaches 5/5 at the end of turn 4. Scarblade Scout, Lys Alana Informant, Dawnhand Eulogist and Trystan put Elf cards there as a side effect of being bodies you wanted to play anyway, and Nameless Inversion is a changeling removal spell that flips the switch simply by being cast. Morcant's Loyalist converts the resulting board of undercosted Elves into lethal, Champions of the Perfect turns every subsequent creature spell into a card, and Gloom Ripper — whose X counts Elves on the battlefield PLUS Elf cards in the graveyard — turns a stalled attack into a kill. The graveyard here is a switch, not an engine: it is on by turn 2 and never turns off.",
